# The IBEX Knowledge-Base: Achieving more together with open science

**Authors:** Andrea J. Radtke, Ifeanyichukwu Anidi, Leanne Arakkal, Armando Arroyo-Mejias, Rebecca T. Beuschel, Katy Borner, Colin J. Chu, Beatrice Clark, Menna R. Clatworthy, Jake Colautti, Joshua Croteau, Saven Denha, Rose Dever, Walderez O. Dutra, Sonja Fritzsche, Spencer Fullam, Michael Y. Gerner, Anita Gola, Kenneth J. Gollob, Jonathan M. Hernandez, Jyh Liang Hor, Hiroshi Ichise, Zhixin Jing, Danny Jonigk, Evelyn Kandov, Wolfgang Kastenmueller, Joshua F. E. Koenig, Aanandita Kothurkar, Alexandra Y. Kreins, Ian Lamborn, Yuri Lin, Katia Luciano Pereira Morais, Aleksandra Lunich, Jean C. S. Luz, Ryan B. MacDonald, Chen Makranz, Vivien I. Maltez, Ryan V. Moriaty, Juan M. Ocampo-Godinez, Vitoria M. Olyntho, Kartika Padhan, Kirsten Remmert, Nathan Richoz, Edward C. Schrom, Wanjing Shang, Lihong Shi, Rochelle M. Shih, Emily Speranza, Salome Stierli, Sarah A. Teichmann, Tibor Z. Veres, Megan Vierhout, Brianna T. Wachter, Adam K. Wade-Vallance, Margaret Williams, Nathan Zangger, Ronald N. Germain, Ziv Yaniv

## Summary
Iterative Bleaching Extends multipleXity (IBEX) is a versatile method for highly multiplexed imaging of diverse tissues. Based on open science principles, we created the IBEX Knowledge-Base, a resource for reagents, protocols and more, to empower innovation.


